  "provenance": {
    "pc_animation_steps": "func_08109EF8 selects a PcAnimStep stream through the 14-entry index; callers use constants 0,11,12,13, branch-selected values 5..10, and state values assigned 0..3. func_08109F20 consumes opcode0 steps and advances after duration unk_22; opcode1 restarts at step0 and opcode2 stops. Each independently traversed stream therefore includes its first opcode1/2 terminal record. The 14 derived extents partition 190 real36-byte records without gaps or overlap, ending exactly at the separately declared gUnk_09A4C9EC scalar table. All6840 source-record bytes and every stream count/opcode agree across US,JP,EU. Padding halfwords at2,10,26 are zero. The raw step records are source-level boss animation commands, not encoded graphics, and the index is real runtime data. All names retain the existing US address convention; no pointer casting or synthetic arrays are used.",
    "pc_sprite_commands": "func_0810A018 walks PcSpriteCmd records until flag bit0x80; every native terminal is flag0xFF. The real struct is12 bytes (two u8 fields, four s16 fields, one u16 field). Traversing the96 independently rooted command streams yields4380 full records and exactly partitions52560 native bytes when sorted by physical start. Runtime index order is preserved separately and agrees across regions; it is not assumed to equal physical order. Every index0..95 is used by the previously owned PcAnimStep command selector field, and all command bytes are identical in US,JP,EU. Drawing uses flags, sprite selectors, layer indices and coordinates, so these are program-level command records rather than pixel payload. The96-entry pointer table ends at the separately owned PcAnimStep selector. Existing fallback name gUnk_09A3DF34 and pointer index gUnk_09EF9C34 retain canonical types and public unsized declarations.",
    "pc_graphics_sets": "func_0810A018 consumes PcGfxSet tile pointer/size and background-map pointer/size at offsets0/4 and8/12. Every selector0..42 appears in live opcode0 records of the independently owned PcAnimStep streams, and the43 native16-byte records end at the separately owned first PcAnimStep array in every region. All size fields match across US,JP,EU and the two padding halfwords are zero. Every one of the86 pointed native payloads is byte-identical across the three regions for its declared size, independently corroborating each raw tile/map correspondence. Consecutive tile starts advance by their preceding declared tile sizes; maps advance by2048. These real resource descriptors are program data; their tile and map payloads remain encoded assets.",
    "pc_palette_and_shots": "func_0810A444 initializes palette-cycle state0; func_0810A454 follows the complete1,2,0 successor cycle and indexes the corresponding three durations, all6. Those independently rooted halfword arrays occupy6 bytes each. The shot consumer in func_0810A9CC selects a horizontal category0/1/2 and adds vertical category0/3/6, proving all nine16-byte PcShot records. Their existing const-qualified canonical type is preserved, including zero padding at offset10. All156 bytes match across US,JP,EU and end at the separately owned task_bos_pc registration-name string. These are state-transition/duration and projectile parameters, not encoded graphics.",
    "native_catalog": "The independently bounded sprite-command streams, graphics descriptors, animation-step streams and primary palette-cycle arrays form one contiguous native 60100-byte initialized-data catalog in all regions. They remain in boss_pc_data.c, with ordinary definitions ordered as commands, graphics, animation and palette data. The existing const nine-shot table follows as the native 144-byte readonly section. All existing types, qualifiers, array bounds and initializer values are preserved, including the unused record fields. The actor in bos6.c selects and reads these related catalogs through its existing typed indexes and helpers. No code, pointer interface or asset payload changes. The intervening task_bos_pc name and the following shake/secondary-palette tables retain their existing ownership and placement; this reconstruction does not assert a complete original source boundary or remove their remaining section annotations."
